    run_path_extern_text_corruption_causes_false_gpu_skip_2026-08-20, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep-20261127: all four corruption shapes from the doc (inline val binding, cross-fn parameter, call-result-as-argument, literal concat) verified clean on the fresh HEAD seed under simple run compiled mode AND test mode - len=8 eq=true on every line for both the boxed-value ABI (rt_text_to_lower_ascii) and ptr+len ABI (rt_path_basename). Root cause per doc was one machine word per text operand in the pure-Simple codegen route; fixed at tip by src/compiler/50.mir/text_extern_abi.spl text_arg_indices + MIR-level split in switch_operators_calls.spl:1425 (rt_string_data/rt_string_len); the green guard text_extern_abi_ptr_len_registry_spec 5/5 PASS. The false-GPU-skip half is also converted at HEAD (zero assert_true(probe_result.starts_with(skip:)) sites; gpu_lane_probe_verdict everywhere). Added test/02_integration/compiler/backend/run_path_extern_text_return_abi_native_spec.spl (+ fixture test/fixtures/compiler/run_path_extern_text_return/main.spl) asserting byte-exact stdout from a native-built binary, with the skip-on-seed contract identical to its sibling; both skip paths verified byte-identical reporting. Residuals flagged for owners: stale RED text_extern_abi_ptr_len_divergence_spec (asserts the backend alone splits raw-MIR operands - impossible under the landed MIR-split architecture; re-aim or retire per compiler-core owner); vulkan_jit_hello_spec Windows false-run (gpu_lane owner); final pure-Simple-producer parity pending the admitted self-hosted compiler per the doc. close_evidence reproducer=test/02_integration/compiler/backend/run_path_extern_text_return_abi_native_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/backend/text_extern_abi_ptr_len_registry_spec.spl"

